[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/talk/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n0_traveller_road"
text = "# DRAFT
# The traveller beside the porter on the carter's wagon, night 0: Will Fuller, a wool merchant from Colchester, forty-one, bound for Cheapside, inside the walls. A wife and two girls at home. Wry, warm, more frightened than he lets on.
# He turns to the porter himself a little way down the road (the Fields cue), and the porter can turn to him again on the road in (E): that starts at again.
# One turn to him is one talk: after each answer the questions left come up again, until the porter turns away or has asked them all.
# Before the cart he only hints at the abbey: road talk, men who don't come home. When the cart with the dead comes close he breaks this talk off himself (traveller.tres says the rest), with no parting line; at Aldgate he breaks off again to greet the warden.
# After the cart (talked_n0_traveller) the porter can ask what he thinks goes on in the abbey, whether he's been inside, what people say, and who would know more. Nothing on the ride reveals a demon or men behind the deaths. After Aldgate (n0_past_aldgate) he opens on the warden.
== start
-> after [if talked_n0_traveller]
-> hello

== hello
Traveller: Evening, brother. Bound for the city, are you?
* I'm to be porter at an abbey inside Aldgate. -> porter
* Where are you bound yourself? -> trade
* (Nod, and say nothing.) -> quiet

== quiet [set n0_road_quiet]
Traveller: Not one for talk. (He blows into his hands.) Then I'll talk for both of us. It keeps the cold out.
Traveller: Wool, for Cheapside. Twelve days on the road from Colchester, and every one of them wet.
-> topics

== porter [set n0_road_porter]
Traveller: The porter? At the abbey in the lane, by the Cross Keys?
Traveller: (He looks at you a moment longer than he needs to.) Well. Somebody has to keep the gate.
Traveller: You look young for it. They give that work to old men, mostly. Men with nothing left to want.
* I'm nineteen. Old enough. -> young
* The old porter went blind. They needed someone. -> blind
* I go where my abbot sends me. -> sent

== young [set n0_road_young]
Traveller: Nineteen. (He laughs, not unkindly.) At nineteen I was sure I'd be rich by thirty.
Traveller: I'm forty-one, and sat in the back of a cart in the rain. Keep your vows, brother. They're cheaper than wool.
-> topics

== blind [set n0_road_blind]
Traveller: Blind, was he. (He's quiet a moment.) Years on a gate, watching who comes in after dark.
Traveller: I'd not want to know what a man sees, all those years. Maybe the eyes just give up.
-> topics

== sent [set n0_road_sent]
Traveller: Obedience. My father wanted that of me, and I gave him a wool trade instead.
Traveller: Your abbot, now. Does he know the house he's sending you to?
* He says it's a holy house. It has a saint. -> holy
* I don't think he knows it at all. -> unknown

== holy
Traveller: A saint. Yes. Everyone on this road has heard of the saint.
(He says it the way a man says the name of a dog that bit him.)
-> topics

== unknown
Traveller: Then that's two of you. Three, with me.
-> topics

== trade [set n0_road_trade]
Traveller: Cheapside, with wool. I buy it cheap in Colchester and sell it dear in London.
Traveller: Every toll on the road robs me in between. The bridges, the gates, the bishop's men. A sack's half sold before it's sold.
* Is it a good living? -> living
* Have you family at home? -> family
* (Let him grumble.) -> topics

== living [set n0_road_living]
Traveller: Good enough to complain about. (He pats the bale under him.) This is a winter's bread for my house.
Traveller: Which is why I'll sleep inside the walls tonight, and not in some ditch.
-> topics

== family [set n0_road_family]
Traveller: A wife, and two girls who think London's paved with ribbon. I'm to bring them some.
Traveller: (His face goes quiet.) My wife made me swear I'd stop nowhere but an inn I know. She's heard the stories too.
* What stories? -> stories
* (Nod.) -> topics

== stories [set n0_road_stories]
Traveller: Road talk. Men who set out for London and don't come home. There are always some.
Traveller: (He glances at the carter's back.) More, this year. Ask him why he whips his horse when the light goes.
-> topics

== carter [set n0_road_carter]
Traveller: They shut the city gates at the curfew bell. Be on the wrong side and you sleep in the ditch.
Traveller: He doesn't care to sleep in a ditch. Not this month.
-> topics

== name [set n0_road_name]
Traveller: Will Fuller. Will, to anyone who's shared a wet cart with me.
Traveller: And you're brother something, and you'll tell me if you like. I'll not press a monk.
* Alric. -> alric
* (Smile, and leave it.) -> topics

== alric [set n0_road_alric]
Traveller: Alric. (He tries it.) Well, Brother Alric. I'll pray for you, if you'll pray for my wool.
-> topics

== topics
-> spent [if n0_road_porter] [if n0_road_trade] [if n0_road_carter] [if n0_road_stories] [if n0_road_name]
-> topics_late [if n0_road_porter] [if n0_road_trade]
-> topics_early

== topics_early
* [if not n0_road_porter] I'm to be porter at an abbey inside Aldgate. -> porter
* [if not n0_road_trade] Where are you bound yourself? -> trade
* [if not n0_road_carter] Is the carter always in such a hurry? -> carter

== topics_late
* [if not n0_road_name] I never asked your name. -> name
* [if not n0_road_carter] Is the carter always in such a hurry? -> carter
* [if not n0_road_stories] What's different about this year? -> stories

== again
-> after [if talked_n0_traveller]
-> spent [if n0_road_porter] [if n0_road_trade] [if n0_road_carter] [if n0_road_stories] [if n0_road_name]
-> still

== still
Traveller: Brother? (He shifts on the sacks.) Go on, ask. It shortens the road.
-> topics

== spent
Traveller: (He pulls his hood closer.) Save your breath, brother. It's a cold way to Aldgate yet.
-> end

== after
-> after_gate [if n0_past_aldgate]
Traveller: Still thinking of that cart, brother? So am I.
-> after_topics

== after_gate
Traveller: (He watches the gate's light go small behind you.) He took his time over you, that warden. Most nights they wave a monk through.
-> after_topics

== after_topics
-> after_spent [if n0_road_think] [if n0_cart_say] [if n0_road_ask]
-> after_ask

== after_ask
* [if not n0_road_think] What do you think goes on in that abbey? -> think
* [if not n0_cart_say] What do people say about it? -> say
* [if not n0_road_ask] Who would know more? -> ask

== think [set n0_road_think]
Traveller: I think men go in at that gate to pray, and nobody sees them come out.
Traveller: That's all I know, and it's more than I want to. I'd call it a reason to keep walking.
* Those are my brothers you're talking about. -> defend
* Have you been inside? -> inside
* (Say nothing.) -> after_topics

== defend [set n0_road_defend]
Traveller: I'm talking about a wall I can't see over. (He shrugs.) You'll be over it tomorrow. Then you tell me.
-> after_topics

== inside [set n0_road_inside]
Traveller: Once, at Lent, to see the saint. A finger in a glass box, and more candles than I've seen in my life.
Traveller: And cold. Cold in there like the bottom of a well. I said my prayer and I didn't stay.
-> after_topics

== say [set n0_cart_say]
Traveller: (He opens his mouth, and shuts it again.) People say a good many things, brother. None of them in daylight.
Traveller: You'll hear it all at the Keys tonight, I don't doubt. I'd rather not be the one who told you.
-> after_topics

== ask [set n0_road_ask]
Traveller: The inn across the lane from the abbey gate. The Cross Keys.
Traveller: Buy the landlord an ale and he'll talk till the candle's out. His wife hears more, and says less.
-> after_topics

== after_spent
Traveller: I've said more than I meant to, brother. (He tries a smile.) It's the cold. It loosens a man.
-> end

== leave
Traveller: Suit yourself, brother.
"
